# Force LF everywhere. This repo is authored on Windows but every artefact in it
# is consumed by Linux: the shell scripts run under bash, and everything under
# os/files/ is copied verbatim into the OS image.
#
# Without this, git's autocrlf would hand out CRLF on checkout, and a script with
# a trailing \r in its shebang fails as "bad interpreter" while a systemd or bootc
# config with CRLF is parsed wrong or silently ignored. We already lost time to
# exactly this failure mode once, via a CRLF-terminated SSH key that made
# bootc-image-builder reject its own TOML.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Belt and braces for the files that would hurt most.
*.sh        text eol=lf
*.toml      text eol=lf
*.conf      text eol=lf
*.yml       text eol=lf
Containerfile text eol=lf

# Disk images, archives and artwork must never be touched.
*.vhdx      binary
*.qcow2     binary
*.raw       binary
*.iso       binary
*.bmp       binary
*.png       binary
*.ttf       binary
*.woff2     binary

# Historical upstream patch evidence retains its original context whitespace.
*.patch     -whitespace
